{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.6,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["D37", "D40", "D42"],
      "pins": ["D37.2", "D40.2", "D42.2"],
      "nets": ["/NET0175"],
      "observed": "The anodes of three LEDs (D37 green, D40 green, D42 yellow) sit on net /NET0175 and nothing else. No supply, pull-up or driver is connected to that net. Their cathodes drive the Ethernet and PI status lines through R73, R98 and R82.",
      "expected": "Status LED anodes need a supply reference (here +3V3, as with D2, D5, D46 and D14). The Ethernet link/activity LEDs driven by the CM4 open-collector nLED pins cannot light without it.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"36\") (name \"/NET0175\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"D37\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"D40\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"D42\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A\") (pintype \"passive\")))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"R98\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")) ... (node (ref \"D40\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"K\") (pintype \"passive\"))"}
      ],
      "impact": "The three status LEDs never illuminate, so the Ethernet activity and PI activity indication is lost. The board's behaviour is otherwise unaffected.",
      "confidence": 0.5
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["U9"],
      "pins": ["U9.10"],
      "nets": [],
      "observed": "U9 (LIS3MDL magnetometer) pin 10 (~{CS}) does not appear on any net. Its sibling IMU U50 (LSM6DS3) has its CS pin tied to +3V3 (net 1).",
      "expected": "The LIS3MDL CS pin must be tied to Vdd_IO for I2C operation. Leaving it floating makes the interface mode undefined.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"U50\") (pin \"12\") (pinfunction \"CS\") (pintype \"input\"))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(libpart (lib \"Sensor_Magnetic\") (part \"LIS3MDL\") ... (pin (num \"10\") (name \"~{CS}\") (type \"input\"))"}
      ],
      "impact": "The magnetometer may not reliably enter I2C mode, so it may fail to respond on the I2C bus at GPIO22/GPIO23.",
      "confidence": 0.4
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["R17"],
      "pins": ["R17.1", "R17.2"],
      "nets": ["VOUTN", "VOUTP"],
      "observed": "R17 is valued 24k, but its description and LCSC part (C2930261, FRC0805J240TSD) describe a 24Ω resistor. The value and part identity disagree.",
      "expected": "The value should match the purchased part. A 24Ω part placed across the bipolar rails would not match a 24k value.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(comp (ref \"R17\") (value \"24k\") ... (description \" 125mW Thick Film Resistors 150V ±5% 24Ω 0805 Chip Resistor - Surface Mount ROHS\")"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(field (name \"LCSC\") \"C2930261\") (field (name \"MPN\") \"FRC0805J240TSD\")"}
      ],
      "impact": "If the 24Ω part is fitted, it loads the VOUTN/VOUTP supply heavily, which changes rail voltages and dissipation. If the 24k value is intended, the BOM part is wrong.",
      "confidence": 0.3
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist shows three status LED anodes tied to a net with no supply, a floating chip-select on the LIS3MDL magnetometer, and a resistor whose value conflicts with its described part. The first two are the most likely real connection faults; the resistor finding is weaker."
}

